    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 30-layer HfO2/SiO2 multilayer coating on fused silica substrate at normal incidence with unpolarized illumination. Stack topology: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | ... (alternating, 15 bilayer pairs, 30 total finite layers) | Fused Silica. Initialize layer thicknesses using quarter-wave optical thickness at 375 nm for HfO2 and SiO2 layers in the first 10 pairs (UV reflector region), and at 1350 nm for remaining 5 pairs (SWIR transmitter region). Apply ±15% uniform random jitter to all seed thicknesses. Set individual layer thickness optimization bounds: 20 nm minimum, 500 nm maximum. Constrain outermost SiO2 layer thickness >= 200 nm. Optimize all 30 layer thicknesses simultaneously to maximize average transmittance in 1000-1700 nm band and maximize average reflectance in 300-450 nm band. Use gradient-based optimizer with increased initial population sampling density (2x baseline). Evaluate spectrum from 300-1700 nm at 5 nm resolution. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: low transmission in 300-450 nm; low reflection in 1000-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30; materials restricted to HfO2 and SiO2.",
